[{:adr/authoritative_for ["follow-up to ADR-2607102700 (Phase 1 landing): acts on that ADR's own\n    methodological note that independent review should follow any non-trivial\n    GTG landing as standard practice, not an optional extra" "landed 2026-07-09: kotoba-lang/standard-model#11 merged as\n    6296794a5eb5bec816e76994336685f453fc9012, 77 tests/2898 assertions, CI\n    green (JDK17+21, after one transient infra retry -- 504 gateway timeout\n    downloading Clojure CLI tooling, unrelated to code); superproject pin\n    advanced via API single-entry commit 89edb0d773d9d40d089d2df2efcd6754b38c2e6b" "BUG: curvature-scalar computed gamma^a.(gamma^b.R(h_b^h_a)), contracting\n    the ALREADY-COVARIANT riemann-basis-pair (eq 4.48, already built FROM h via\n    L_a=a.hbar(grad)) against wedge(h_b,h_a) -- position-gauge-field ROWS --\n    instead of fixed frame basis vectors e_a^e_b per eq (4.11)/(4.12). Since\n    riemann-basis-pair already IS the covariant R (eq 4.9, R(B)=R(h(B)) for\n    flat R + basis B), this applied h a SECOND time" "why CI-green Schwarzschild verification missed it: existing test checked\n    only the SCALAR (trace). LDG's own Schwarzschild solution has\n    h(e_1)=e_1,h(e_2)=e_2,h(e_3)=e_3 exactly (fixed points), so double-h is a\n    no-op on purely-spatial pairs and only affects index-0 terms; the\n    resulting genuinely-asymmetric ~1e-4-magnitude Ricci-TENSOR components\n    (~2000x above the ~1e-10 FD-noise floor) happened to cancel in this\n    solution's trace specifically -- independently reconfirmed by the\n    requester (not just re-reading the reviewer's report) via a fresh REPL\n    computation of the full tensor: buggy R_10~1.9e-4 vs R_01~9e-11\n    (physically-impossible asymmetry, Ricci tensor must be symmetric) vs\n    fixed formula uniformly ~1e-10 (correct)" "THIRD occurrence of this exact failure mode in this repo's GTG work (after\n    PR #6 structure-constant slot order, and Phase 1's own first\n    implementation attempt using the wrong covariant derivative) -- a\n    seemingly-thorough single pass, confidently silently wrong, invisible to\n    'tests pass', caught only by independent numeric verification against a\n    ground truth STRONGER than the existing regression check" "FIX: riemann-basis-pair(b,a) called directly, no wedge-vectors/general\n    riemann-map needed (both indices always fixed basis vectors here, never\n    h-field rows). Argument order (b,a) vs (a,b) is explicitly disclosed in\n    the docstring as ONLY algebraically justified (re-derived from eq\n    4.11/4.12 structure), NOT independently numerically confirmed -- since\n    riemann-basis-pair is antisymmetric and the only available verification\n    (Schwarzschild) has R=0 identically, a sign error would be numerically\n    invisible; honest caveat pending a literature worked example with a\n    NONZERO known value or independent expert review of the derivation. The\n    MAGNITUDE fix (the actual bug) IS independently numerically confirmed by\n    two people from scratch; the sign convention is not" "added curvature-scalar-full-ricci-tensor-vanishes-not-merely-its-trace: a\n    strictly stronger regression test checking every Ricci tensor component\n    (not just trace) at both Schwarzschild points -- exactly the check that\n    would have caught this bug at Phase 1's original landing" "scope check: frame-adjoint, H-field, omega-from-h, L-a-omega,\n    riemann-basis-pair, riemann-map/riemann-map-matrix all independently\n    RE-confirmed correct by the same review (multiple methods including a\n    from-scratch Dirac-gamma-matrix verification path, kotoba.sm.spinor/gammas,\n    fully independent of the FD-based riemann-map code path) -- bug isolated\n    to curvature-scalar's final assembly step only" "methodological consequence: this is now the THIRD instance of this failure\n    mode -- future GTG phases should treat independent adversarial review\n    immediately after any non-trivial landing as standard operating procedure,\n    and prefer regression tests checking the STRONGEST available invariant\n    (here: full tensor) over the weakest convenient one (here: trace) when\n    they are not provably equivalent under available test data -- they\n    coincided here only because R=0 (vacuum) makes both vanish, a coincidence\n    of the vacuum case not a general equivalence" "explicitly out of scope, unchanged: everything ADR-2607102300/2607102700\n    already declared out of scope (matter coupling, Einstein multivector,\n    GR-equivalence proof beyond Schwarzschild, quantization/RGE/scattering/\n    lattice, dark-sector/de-Sitter) -- this ADR fixes a bug in already-in-scope\n    code, does not widen scope"], :adr/supersedes [], :adr/superseded_by [], :adr/topic "kotoba-lang-standard-model", :adr/related ["adr-2607102700" "adr-2607102300" "adr-2607101900" "adr-2607101700"], :adr/status "accepted", :adr/id "adr-2607103000-kotoba-lang-standard-model-curvature-scalar-double-h-bug-fix", :adr/doc_type "adr", :adr/last_verified "2026-07-09", :adr/body "see 2607103000-kotoba-lang-standard-model-curvature-scalar-double-h-bug-fix.md", :adr/deciders ["Jun Kawasaki"], :adr/date "2026-07-09", :db/id -1, :adr/authoritative true, :adr/title "ADR-2607103000: kotoba-lang/standard-model — curvature-scalar double-applied h; fixed by the independent review the previous landing ADR called for"}]